If you need more control, you can create a wrapper type that implements `slog.LogValuer`<p><pre><code>    type StringerValue struct {
        fmt.Stringer
    }

    func (v StringerValue) LogValue() slog.Value {
        return slog.StringValue(v.String())
    }

</code></pre>
Usage example:<p><pre><code>    slog.Any(&quot;requests&quot;, StringerValue{req})

</code></pre>
There might be a case for making the expvar types implement `slog.LogValuer` directly.
